I heard many positive results of XSA, but also heard a lot of negative results. Interesting.

@classiclarryd: "New NanoGPT speedrun world record at 81.2 seconds, a 0.6-second improvement, using learnable XSA. This involves a per-head learnable scalar to subtract out the portion of attention orthogonal to a token's own value vector, applied to the six non-paired head layers."

The linked GitHub pull request reports a NanoGPT (124M parameters) training run that achieves this speed in 90 seconds, demonstrating the efficiency gains possible with XSA gating layers.

